	<description>Written in 1914 but not published until 1925, a year after Kafka’s death, &lt;i&gt;The Trial &lt;/i&gt;is the terrifying tale of Josef K., a respectable bank officer who is suddenly and inexplicably arrested and must defend himself against a charge about which he can get no information. Whether read as an existential tale, a parable, or a prophecy of the excesses of modern bureaucracy wedded to the madness of totalitarianism, &lt;i&gt;The Trial &lt;/i&gt;has resonated with chilling truth for generations of readers.</description>
